WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:06.020
Hollywood has been plotting a remake of Katsuhiro
Otomo's Akira for almost two decades.

00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:11.500
The project has a complicated and somewhat
controversial history, but Leonardo DiCaprio

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.640
remains attached as producer, and he seems
determined to make the live-action Akira a

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.180
reality.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.480
We’ve got all the details right here.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:25.900
When Akira dropped in 1988, bootleg copies
spread across U.S. campuses like wildfire.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.900
Leonardo DiCaprio was a teenager when Akira
hit the States, and it clearly made a big

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:31.640
impression on him.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.780
The Oscar winner has been a big fan of anime
for years now, Akira in particular.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:43.040
His production company Appian Way got involved
with the Warner Bros.-led remake back in 2008,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.880
and the first thing DiCaprio did was put the
fans at ease.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.160
He told MTV:

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.620
"I'm a big fan of Japanese anime.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:54.270
[...] I know there's a lot of loyal fans out
there of the project and die-hard fans, so

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:58.820
we're going to try to do the best job we possibly
can and we're not going to make the movie

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.260
until the script is in the right shape."

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.780
After Earth writer Gary Whitta was the man
tasked with penning the screenplay.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:10.380
According to Whitta, an Akira trilogy was
being quietly planned, but the first installment

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:10.940
faltered.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:17.080
Director Ruairi Robinson, best known for 2013
sci-fi The Last Days on Mars, later revealed

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.320
that producers put the project on the back-burner
for financial reasons.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.220
He said:

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:26.040
"They couldn't get the budget under 200 million
bucks for that draft, which was a bit rich

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.140
for what was proposed as an R-rated movie
with no stars."

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:34.400
Warner Bros. had Robinson put together a sizzle
reel, and the Irish filmmaker even shot some

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:38.320
test footage for the film, recreating some
iconic Akira shots.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.400
Akira takes place three decades after Tokyo
is leveled by a devastating explosion.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:52.900
The mega city that springs up in the aftermath
is Neo-Tokyo, home to the young biker gang

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.320
that the story revolves around.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.740
When one of the boys develops powerful psychokinetic
abilities, the city faces destruction all

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:00.300
over again.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.460
It's a big-budget story, which is probably
why DiCaprio and his partners at Warner Bros.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.560
decided to film the whole movie in California.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:15.020
Making Akira totally in-state means it qualifies
for an 18.5 million dollar tax credit allocation,

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.280
Warner Bros. confirmed.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.100
The studio told Deadline:

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.900
“We are thrilled with the opportunity to
shoot Akira in California.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.840
The availability of top-notch crew members,
plus the wide variety of location choices

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.780
and predictable weather are second to none.”

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.140
Needless to say, fans of the original are
deeply concerned about this move.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.740
The setting and aesthetic of Akira are central
to its appeal, and recreating this in the

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.020
Golden State won’t be easy.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:45.680
Taika Waititi was attached to the Akira remake
before his first Marvel movie made him a household

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:46.480
name in Hollywood.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:52.800
The New Zealander opened up about his plans
for Akira while promoting 2017’s Thor: Ragnarok,

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.500
revealing that he intends to take inspiration
from Otomo’s original manga, not the anime.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.480
Waititi told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.060
"Who wants to see a shot-for-shot remake of
the film?

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:03.660
Nobody.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.760
Also, you have to make it entertaining.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:09.540
I think it's really dangerous to make these
films very serious cyber punk.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:14.920
There was a time and place for that and there
may be a time and place for that tone again,

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.180
but you have to make fresh takes on things."

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:23.380
Waititi is reportedly co-writing the movie
with Always Be My Maybe scribe, Michael Golamco.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.520
When Dazed caught up with Waititi in 2018,
he revealed that the script was still in the

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.780
early stages of development.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:30.320
He said:

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:33.260
"I haven't really started to get my head around
it yet.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.970
There are six gigantic books to go through.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:36.820
It's so rich.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:42.190
But Akira is one of my favorite films; my
mum took me to see it when I was 13 and it

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:42.720
changed my life."

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:48.200
Filming the movie in the States is one thing,
but setting it there is another entirely.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:53.820
In April 2019, Production Weekly shared what
appeared to be the first synopsis for DiCaprio

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:58.480
and Waititi's Akira, and it made some pretty
grim reading for fans of the source material.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:04.060
There were a ton of fundamental changes, including
moving the action from Neo-Tokyo to Neo-Manhattan.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:05.380
The synopsis read:

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:11.400
"When a young man's telekinesis is discovered
by the military, he is taken in to be turned

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:16.160
into a super weapon and his brother [must]
race to save him before Manhattan is destroyed

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:16.780
by his powers.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:22.350
Kaneda is a bar owner in Neo-Manhattan who
is stunned when his brother Tetsuo is abducted

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:23.340
by Government agents."

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:28.020
Films like John Wick prove that Manhattan
offers the perfect palette for this kind of

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:32.280
story, and some fans may have been willing
to get on board with this had it been the

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.000
only change.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:38.880
In Otomo's story, teenagers Kaneda and Tetsuo
are long-time friends, not brothers.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:44.240
The fact that Kaneda now owns a bar suggests
that he and Tetsuo will be aged up for the

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:48.360
movie, but according to another industry website,
this won’t be the case.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:54.130
Backstage has since released what appears
to be a casting call for Akira, and it reveals

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:58.940
that producers are looking for age appropriate
actors to play Tetsuo and Kaneda, who will

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:01.120
be 17- and 18-years-old in the movie.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:06.280
The whole Neo-Manhattan idea actually dates
back to when Warner Bros. first negotiated

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.320
a deal for Akira in 2002.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:13.300
Blade director Stephen Norrington was hired,
but concerns about his involvement were raised

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:17.470
after he told The Hollywood Reporter that
he planned to make the story, quote, “more

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.460
accessible,” presumably to western audiences.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:24.760
When Norrington departed the project, the
studio turned to Ruairi Robinson and Gary

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.880
Whitta, who tried to remain faithful to the
source material on a technicality.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:33.730
In their version of Akira, Manhattan had been
sold and was legally foreign territory, owned

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:35.100
and populated by the Japanese.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.120
Does this mean the leads would have been Japanese?

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:39.540
Probably not.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:40.940
Whitta told Collider:

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:45.900
"It wasn't New Tokyo, but there were Americans
who kind of lived in little Americanized quarters

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:46.460
of it.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:53.180
I felt it was a way to do a kind of cool Western-Eastern
fusion of the two ideas — not fully Japanese,

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.300
not fully westernized."

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:58.500
In other words, he dug the cool bikes and
the whole cyberpunk thing, but he wanted a

00:05:58.540 --> 00:05:59.780
Hollywood star to lead the charge.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:10.640
Keanu Reeves once came very close to playing
the part of Kaneda in the live action Akira

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:11.080
movie.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:15.780
When the Robinson-Whitta version fell through,
Warner Bros. hired Book of Eli co-director

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:19.000
Albert Hughes and Harry Potter screenwriter
Steve Kloves.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:24.100
Reeves became their target, but despite some
constructive talks, the Matrix star ultimately

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:24.960
decided to pass.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:30.830
It was a huge blow for the project - Warner
Bros. reportedly shut down Akira's pre-viz

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:34.220
department and sent most of the staff it had
working on the film home.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:39.060
It turns out Reeves wasn’t the first actor
the studio contacted about the role of Kaneda.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:44.360
Warner Bros. reportedly reached out to Garrett
Hedlund, Chris Pine, Michael Fassbender, Joaquin

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:48.960
Phoenix and even Justin Timberlake, while
Robert Pattinson, Andrew Garfield and James

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:52.420
McAvoy were said to be in contention for the
role of Tetsuo.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:58.240
When fans discovered that a version of Akira
starring Justin Timberlake was a very real

00:06:58.240 --> 00:06:59.700
possibility, they lashed out.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:04.780
One person who was particularly vocal about
the all-white shortlist of actors was George

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:05.340
Takei.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:10.060
The Star Trek legend predicted that Warner
Bros. would have a huge bomb on its hands

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:11.160
if it whitewashed Akira.

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:12.420
He told The Advocate:

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:16.900
"If they're going to do that, why don't they
do something original, because what they do

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:17.560
is offend Asians.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.540
[...] The tradition in Hollywood has always
been to buy a project, change it completely

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:23.320
and flop with it.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:28.100
I think it’s pointless, so I thought I would
save Warner Bros. a bit of failure by warning

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:31.040
them of what will most likely happen if they
continue in that vein.”

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:36.700
This is exactly what happened to Paramount
after it cast Scarlett Johansson as The Major

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:40.100
in its remake of ‘90s anime classic, Ghost
in the Shell.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:45.640
The studio ultimately admitted that the whitewashing
backlash badly hurt the movie, which was a

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:46.320
critical and commercial failure.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:51.180
It seems like Warner Bros. is heeding the
signs - a casting call put out by the studio

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:54.980
appeared to confirm that it was looking for
Asian actors for the lead roles.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:08:01.360
Run A ll Night director Jaume Collet-Serra
replaced Albert Hughes in 2011, but it wasn't

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:02.700
long before he hit a brick wall.

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:07.600
He was already working with a reduced budget
of 90 million dollars, and sources suggested

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:12.420
that Warner Bros. wanted to drop that figure
again, aiming to spend as little as 60 million

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:13.060
on Akira.

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:18.060
In 2014, Collet-Serra confirmed that he was
still trying to get a scaled-down version

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:18.600
made.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:23.280
Unfortunately, the Spanish director also made
some incredibly ill-advised comments about

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:23.920
Otomo's story.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:25.540
He told Coming Soon:

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.220
"Nobody's interesting.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:32.400
Tetsuo's interesting because weird s--- happens
to him, and Kaneda is so two-dimensional.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:36.620
That's part of the Japanese culture, they
never have strong characters.

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:39.840
They're used as a way to move the other philosophy
forward."

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:43.780
Unsurprisingly, Collet-Serra soon found himself
out of the picture.

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:49.040
Jordan Peele was linked to Akira not long
after his Oscar-winning directorial debut

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:54.060
Get Out premiered, though he quickly decided
that taking charge of a Hollywood remake wasn’t

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:55.020
for him.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:09:00.120
The actor and filmmaker told horror website
The 13th Floor that he was capable of directing

00:09:00.129 --> 00:09:02.559
the new Akira, he just didn’t want to.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:03.400
Peele said:

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:08.209
"Akira is one of my favorite movies, and I
think obviously the story justifies as big

00:09:08.209 --> 00:09:09.880
a budget as you can possibly dream of.

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:16.240
But the real question for me is: Do I want
to do pre-existing material, or do I want

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:16.800
to do original content?

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.760
At the end of the day, I want to do original
stuff."

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:23.660
Peele’s rejection came on the back of George
Miller declaring himself out.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:28.540
The Australian director was asked about Akira
after 2015’s Mad Max: Fury Road became a

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:32.080
roaring success, but he couldn’t fit it
into his busy schedule.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.460
He told Yahoo:

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:34.760
“There was talk of [Akira].

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:38.500
But I’ve got so many things on my dance
card, I don’t have the time to do everything."

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:45.380
In May 2019, Akira fans got some much-needed
good news regarding the long-gestating live-action

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:48.760
adaptation — Warner Bros. had finally set
a release date.

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:55.020
Taika Waititi's film was going to hit cineplexes
on May 21, 2021, the studio confirmed, but

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:57.760
another huge development was just around the
corner.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:04.080
In July 2019, news that Waititi had agreed
a deal to helm another Thor movie broke.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:08.820
It was great news for Marvel fans, but it
was a cruel blow for those who have been waiting

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:10.160
patiently for Akira.

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:15.160
The proposed schedule for Thor: Love &amp; Thunder
clashed with that of Akira, and the latter

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:18.680
film was put on hold indefinitely as a result.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:24.000
Waititi remains attached, but Akira is now
back in limbo, and the headache continues.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:37.280
Any new version of Akira still has to go through
Katsuhiro Otomo.

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:43.059
When the Japanese artist, writer and director
sat down with Forbes in 2017, he revealed

00:10:43.059 --> 00:10:47.540
that he was, quote, “basically done” with
Akira, having finished his original manga

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.420
and helmed his very own anime version.

00:10:50.309 --> 00:10:55.320
Otomo confirmed that he's happy for a new
filmmaker to take Akira in a different direction,

00:10:55.329 --> 00:10:57.509
so long as he gets final approval.

00:10:57.509 --> 00:10:58.080
He said:

00:10:58.509 --> 00:11:03.660
"I accepted the offer for a live-action Akira
to be made, so I am generally okay with whatever

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:04.540
they want to do with it.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:10.740
However, I did give one major condition to
a live-action version and that is that I had

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:12.520
to check and approve the scenario.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:17.720
As always, the fundamental question on adapting
anything is whether you follow the host work

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:19.700
strictly or do something new with it."

